      "title": "Assistant Rowing Coach I (Part-time, 19 hours per week)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-23\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Description: Who We Are Seattle Pacific University is a Christian university fully committed to engaging the culture and changing the world by graduating people of competence and character, becoming people of wisdom, and modeling grace-filled community. Seattle Pacific Athletics is committed to developing champions in competition, in the classroom, and in life. As a member of NCAA Division II and the Great Northwest Athletic Conference (GNAC), SPU Athletics emphasizes excellence, integrity, service, and Christian character. The Women's Rowing program provides student-athletes with a highly competitive and supportive environment where they can grow as athletes, students, and leaders. What We Need: Seattle Pacific University is seeking an enthusiastic and driven individual to join our Women’s Rowing team as a part-time Assistant Coach. This role is ideal for someone eager to grow within NCAA rowing while playing a pivotal role in recruiting, mentoring, and leading student-athletes toward competitive success. The ideal candidate will be a strong communicator, team player, and positive role model who thrives in a faith-centered educational environment. The Assistant Rowing Coach position supports Seattle Pacific University’s mission by contributing to a Christ‑centered learning and working community committed to academic excellence, service, and engagement with the world. In this role, the employee brings their skills, gifts, and professional expertise to work that matters—serving students, colleagues, and the broader University community in ways that reflect SPU’s values and purpose. To that end, all University employees are required to be aligned with and supportive of SPU's Statement of Faith and its derivative policies and lifestyle expectations. What You’ll Do: Lead, mentor, and support student-athletes with integrity and enthusiasm Recruit prospective student-athletes both from high schools and from the on-campus community Instruct rowing fundamentals and foster development of novice rowers into varsity contributors Collaborate with the Head Coach and other staff to deliver safe, successful team experiences Assist with administrative tasks and logistical operations Participate in spring travel and weekend events as required Help with rowing equipment maintenance and boathouse upkeep Represent SPU Athletics with professionalism and positivity   What You Bring: Education:  Bachelor’s degree required Experience:  Experience with a competitive collegiate rowing program (as athlete or coach) Skills & Characteristics: Strong interpersonal and leadership abilities Initiative and commitment to athlete development and recruitment Enthusiasm for collaborative team culture and student mentorship Interest in learning and growing as a collegiate coach Certifications (or willingness to obtain post-hire with SPU support): CPR Certification Washington State Boater’s License Washington State Driver’s License USRowing Level 2 Certification   Mission Alignment:  You have a personal commitment to Christian faith, enthusiasm about supporting SPU's mission , alignment with the University's Statement of Faith , and willingness to accept the lifestyle standards of the Christian community. ​ Appointment Details: Salary Range: $25,000 - $31,000 annually for 10 month appt, DOE Position Type: Part-Time, Exempt Hours: Approx. 19 hours per week; mornings preferred Start Date: Mid September End Date: Mid June Why SPU? Seattle Pacific University’s beautiful campus is nestled in North Queen Anne, just minutes from downtown Seattle. The Women’s Rowing program enjoys direct access to our on-campus boathouse and daily practices on the protected waters of the Seattle Ship Canal and Lake Union. SPU’s rowing team has experienced significant growth and success and is poised for continued excellence with institutional support and a strong vision for the future. Additional Information: Ready to Apply? Submit your application online through Workday, including a cover letter and resume. We look forward to hearing how you can contribute to the success and spirit of SPU Rowing."
